# admin-ui environment variables
# Copy to .env.local and fill in values for local development.
# Never commit .env.local or any file with real secrets.

# admin-ui has no direct BACKEND calls of its own (T13,
# specs/004-auth-roles-permissions) — authenticated calls to the auth
# service's admin API go through the shared `shell/session` module
# (VITE_AUTH_URL / VITE_API_URL live in shell/.env.example, not here).

# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY — admin-ui's FIRST own import.meta.env.VITE_* var
# (T7/T16, specs/012-employee-address, ADR-0032). A PUBLIC, browser-exposed
# key for Google Places API (New) + Maps JavaScript API, used ONLY by the
# employee-address Street/address suggestion combobox on the Users detail
# screen. Called browser-direct from admin-ui — never proxied through `auth`
# (ADR-0032 decision #1: the identity service must never carry a third
# party's latency on the suite's critical path).
#
# Restriction posture (infra/README.md has the full provisioning runbook):
#   - Application restriction = HTTP referrers listing the SHELL's origins
#     (https://operai.welld.io/*, http://localhost:5173/*, the shell's Vercel
#     preview pattern) — NOT admin-ui's own origin. admin-ui runs as a
#     federated remote inside the shell's document (ADR-0006), so the
#     `Referer` header on every Google call is the shell's top-level URL.
#     Getting this wrong fails 100% of requests, and fails INVISIBLY (AC-3.2's
#     silent-degradation posture) — see plan.md Risk R2.
#   - API restriction = Places API (New) + Maps JavaScript API ONLY.
#   - A daily quota cap + budget alert (Risk R4) — this key's exposure risk
#     is quota/billing theft, never data (it grants nothing but address
#     lookups).
#
# Absence degrades gracefully, never breaks: with this unset, the address
# section falls back to a plain manual-entry form with no suggestion
# affordance (Risk R10) — exactly the same AC-3.2 path a live outage takes.
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# SHELL_REMOTE_URL — build-time dev default for the shell's remoteEntry.js,
# read by vite.config.ts (process.env, NOT import.meta.env — this is a
# Node-side config value, not a browser-side Vite env var). admin-ui consumes
# `shell/session` + `shell/tokens.css` from this URL as a Module Federation
# remote (ADR-0006). Same pattern as refund-ui/estimai-ui's own
# SHELL_REMOTE_URL. Defaults to the shell's pinned local-dev port
# (http://localhost:5173/remoteEntry.js) when unset — override only when
# pointing at a non-default shell instance (e.g. a deployed preview URL).
# SHELL_REMOTE_URL=http://localhost:5173/remoteEntry.js
